T*
(  | sensors | 54 | sensor_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, x_m REAL, y_m REAL |) Tj
T*
(  | readings | 9119212 | sensor_id INTEGER \(FK\), ts TEXT, ts_unix REAL, epoch INTEGER, variable TEXT \(CHECK\),) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(value REAL |) Tj
T*
(  ### Discussion) Tj
T*
(  sensors is loaded from mote_locs.txt but not from SELECT DISTINCT moteid, because those are different) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(lists: only 53 of the 54 deployed motes ever transmitted. readings is long format, which makes it easy) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(to select one channel and cheap to add another variable. One column per channel buys the opposite: the) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(four channels of a reading sit side by side, so comparing a temperature against its own voltage is one) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(WHERE rather than a self-join.) Tj
T*
(  The cost is that every query pays for rows it does not want: query \(a\) needs temperature only but reads all) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(rows to use only 1/4 of them. ts, ts_unix and epoch are each stored four times over.) Tj
T*
(  SQLite has no date type, so the instant is stored twice. ts is fixed-width ISO-8601 in UTC and it sorts) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(chronologically; ts_unix is a number because a RANGE frame needs one. Both tables are STRICT, so a) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(value of the wrong type is rejected instead of being stored anyway.) Tj
T*
(  The natural key is \(sensor_id, ts, variable\). I first tried \(sensor_id, epoch, variable\), which the dataset) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(documentation calls monotonically increasing per mote, but it loses 448435 rows because motes restart) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(the counter after a reboot.) Tj
T*
(  PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON is issued wherever a connection is opened, because it is per-connection and off by) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(default.) Tj
T*
(  ) Tj
T*
(  ## Part 2 Load and Cleaning) Tj
T*
(  ### Results) Tj
T*
(  | rule | rows |) Tj
T*
(  |---|---:|) Tj
T*
(  | in file | 2313682 |) Tj
T*
(  | moteid empty, rejected | 526 |) Tj
T*
(  | moteid outside the 1-54 roster, rejected | 9866 |) Tj
T*
(  | unparseable timestamp or value | 0 |) Tj
T*
(  | accepted | 2303290 |) Tj
T*
(  | empty channel fields, recorded as absent | 93948 |) Tj
T*
(  | readings written | 9119212 |) Tj
T*
(  | foreign key violations | 0 |) Tj
T*
(  Load time 22.2 s. Plausible bounds, applied at read time in query \(d\):) Tj
T*
(  | channel | bound | basis | readings outside |) Tj
T*
(  |---|---|---|---:|) Tj
T*
(  | humidity | 0-100 %RH | dataset doc, "ranging from 0-100%" | 299084 |) Tj
T*
(  | voltage | 2.0-3.0 V | dataset doc, lithium ion, "ranging from 2-3" | 2746 |) Tj
T*
(  | temperature | 0-50 degC | general working environment | 408133 |) Tj
T*
(  | light | 0-2000 lux | observed to saturate at 1847.36 lux | 0 |) Tj
T*
(  ### Discussion) Tj
T*
(  Every row of data.txt has eight fields separated by exactly one space, and a channel that did not arrive) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(leaves its field empty, so two spaces appear in a row. Splitting on a single space keeps that empty) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(field and every row comes out with eight. Splitting on any amount of whitespace, which is what) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(line.split\(\) and pandas do by default, reads those two spaces as one separator, so 93879 rows lose a) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(field and every value after the gap shifts one column left with no error raised. An empty field means) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(the measurement is missing rather than zero, so the loader writes no row for it.) Tj
T*
(  Readings outside these bounds are kept in the database, neither deleted nor marked. The bounds are written) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(directly into query \(d\) and applied when it runs, so changing one gives a different answer without) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(reloading anything.) Tj
T*
(  1847.36 lux is the largest value in the file and repeats 139078 times, far more often than any other, so) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(the sensors reach their maximum there and keep reporting the same number. Everything below that can be) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(real, since some sensors sit near windows, so the bound is set at 2000 rather than lower.) Tj
T*
(  The dying-battery anomalies are counted but not cleaned out. Temperatures outside 0-50 degC come with a) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(voltage averaging 2.19 V in the same transmission, against 2.55 V for the rest. A voltage rule cannot) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(be derived from the temperatures, since the ones that would set it are the corrupted readings) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(themselves; and temperatures cannot be judged by the voltage, since the documentation says the voltage) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(reading itself changes with temperature and over 200000 readings below 2.40 V carry normal) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(temperatures. Dropping everything below some voltage would throw away good data to remove bad.) Tj
T*
(  ) Tj
T*
(  ## Part 3 Indexing) Tj
T*
(  ### Method) Tj
T*
(  The probe query counts the readings from sensor 22 on 2004-03-09. It is run once to warm the cache and then) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(five more times, and the fastest of those five is reported. EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN reports no timings, so) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(the timing comes from time.perf_counter\(\) in Python. The index is created after the load rather than in) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(schema.sql, which is why an unindexed table exists to measure. Both configurations return the same) Tj
T*
